---
/**
 * The qualifying text for `VerifiedBadge` (src/components/VerifiedBadge.tsx),
 * rendered as real, always-visible page content — never a tooltip, never
 * `.visually-hidden` — so it is reachable on touch devices and present in the
 * accessible tree for a screen-reader user who lands directly on the badge
 * (every `VerifiedBadge` on the same page should pass this component's id as
 * its `descriptionId` prop, wiring `aria-describedby` to this paragraph).
 *
 * Every page that renders a `VerifiedBadge` MUST also render exactly one
 * `SignatureNote` (fix/verified-badge-honesty — closes the false "Verified"
 * claim called out against registry.conduitdata.io; see the PR description for
 * the before/after wording). It states plainly what the badge does and does
 * NOT mean:
 *   - what ran: this version's entry in the signed index references a
 *     signature bundle and an SLSA provenance bundle (deriveVerified.ts).
 *   - what did NOT run: this site never downloads the connector binary and
 *     performs no cryptographic check of its own — real verification of the
 *     actual bytes (identity-pinned Sigstore + SLSA provenance) happens at
 *     install time, in the CLI, not here.
 * Real build-time cryptographic verification of the index/artifacts is
 * planned separately (WS4 slices S2/S3) — this component does not claim that
 * work is done.
 */
export const SIGNATURE_NOTE_ID = 'signature-note';
---

<p id={SIGNATURE_NOTE_ID}>
  &ldquo;Signature on file&rdquo; means this version&rsquo;s entry in the registry&rsquo;s signed
  index references a signature bundle and an SLSA provenance bundle &mdash; it does not mean this
  site has cryptographically verified them. This site never downloads the connector binary, so it
  cannot confirm that the file you install today matches what was signed. That check happens when
  you run <code>conduit connectors install &lt;name&gt;</code>, which verifies the actual bytes
  against a pinned publisher identity via Sigstore and checks SLSA provenance before installing
  anything.
</p>
